[WORK]
UID: WORK-GRAMMAR-VIEW-FSM-WIDGET
TITLE: Grammars view: a state-machine widget for the lifecycle, with external events
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The Grammars view renders each type's lifecycle ladder as a state-machine
widget: states are the ladder's own values, and transitions are the moves
the ladder allows between them. The widget should also be able to show the
external events that drive a transition, in the shape
[event:create] -> [state:opened], rather than showing bare states and arrows
with no trigger. A concrete child of the lifecycle redesign tracked in
WORK-GRAMMAR-TAB-LIFECYCLE-VIEW, and a natural consumer of whatever
WORK-SPIKE-TRANSITIONS-SEMANTICS settles on for representing the machine
itself.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Operator, 2026-09-02, verbatim: "grammar view include state machine style
widget for the lifecycle. consider adding external events to the widget.
[event:create] -> [state:opened] kinda thing."
<<<
